import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"HTTP Client/Server Crate Split and Server Runtime","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"HTTP Client/Server Crate Split and Server Runtime","type":"adr","date":"2026-10-28T00:00:00.000Z","status":"accepted","status_note":"Accepted"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"web/project/adrs/archived/0025-http-server.md","filePath":"vendored/web/project/adrs/archived/0025-http-server.md"}`),a={name:`web/project/adrs/archived/0025-http-server.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="http-client-server-crate-split-and-server-runtime" tabindex="-1">HTTP Client/Server Crate Split and Server Runtime <a class="header-anchor" href="#http-client-server-crate-split-and-server-runtime" aria-label="Permalink to “HTTP Client/Server Crate Split and Server Runtime”">​</a></h1><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>The handl runtime currently has a single HTTP capability: <code>handl-lib-http</code> / <code>handl-lib-http-std</code>. These names are client-only, which is now too narrow. The language needs to run <strong>servers</strong> as well — fast, production-grade HTTP servers written in handl and backed by an efficient Rust implementation.</p><p>The VM already supports <code>AsyncFunction</code> and <code>Operation</code> at the <code>Host</code> level, but the module system (<code>Module</code> trait and <code>ModuleHost</code>) only dispatches synchronous <code>Function</code> calls. Exposing an async server module requires the module layer to wire through <code>Host::async_function</code> and <code>Host::operation</code>.</p><p>This ADR scopes the rename, the new server crates, and the staged work needed to make handl a server-authoring language.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><h3 id="_1-rename-the-existing-http-client-crates" tabindex="-1">1. Rename the existing HTTP client crates <a class="header-anchor" href="#_1-rename-the-existing-http-client-crates" aria-label="Permalink to “1. Rename the existing HTTP client crates”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>crates/lib-http</code> → <code>crates/lib-http-client</code> (package <code>handl-lib-http</code> → <code>handl-lib-http-client</code>)</li><li><code>crates/lib-http-std</code> → <code>crates/lib-http-client-std</code> (package <code>handl-lib-http-std</code> → <code>handl-lib-http-client-std</code>)</li><li>Update all <code>Cargo.toml</code> workspace members, dependencies, feature flags, doc comments, and re-exports.</li><li>Preserve all public API names (<code>HttpClient</code>, <code>HttpClientModule</code>, <code>HttpMethod</code>, etc.) and existing <code>ureq</code> implementation.</li></ul><h3 id="_2-extend-module-and-modulehost-to-support-async-operation-dispatch" tabindex="-1">2. Extend <code>Module</code> and <code>ModuleHost</code> to support async/operation dispatch <a class="header-anchor" href="#_2-extend-module-and-modulehost-to-support-async-operation-dispatch" aria-label="Permalink to “2. Extend Module and ModuleHost to support async/operation dispatch”">​</a></h3><p>Before the server module can expose async functions, the module layer must forward them:</p><ul><li>Add <code>Module::async_function</code> and <code>Module::operation</code> default methods returning <code>None</code>.</li><li>Update <code>ModuleHost</code> to implement <code>Host::async_function</code> and <code>Host::operation</code> using the same <code>.</code> split-and-dispatch logic as <code>Host::function</code>.</li><li>Add unit tests in <code>crates/runtime-core</code> proving a module can export an <code>AsyncFunction</code> and an <code>Operation</code>.</li></ul><h3 id="_3-introduce-handl-lib-http-server-abstract-server" tabindex="-1">3. Introduce <code>handl-lib-http-server</code> (abstract server) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_3-introduce-handl-lib-http-server-abstract-server" aria-label="Permalink to “3. Introduce handl-lib-http-server (abstract server)”">​</a></h3><p>The abstract crate defines a platform-agnostic HTTP server interface and an handl module adapter. It has <strong>no I/O</strong> and no platform dependencies, mirroring the client crate pattern.</p><p>Public types:</p><ul><li><code>HttpServer</code> trait — <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>join</code>, <code>route</code>, <code>serve_static</code>, <code>is_running</code>.</li><li><code>HttpServerRequest</code> — method, path, query map, headers, body.</li><li><code>HttpServerResponse</code> — status, headers, body.</li><li><code>HttpMethod</code> (re-exported/aligned with the client crate, or shared in a future <code>lib-http-core</code>).</li><li><code>HttpServerError</code> — network, invalid argument, already running, not running, handler error, with <code>From</code> conversion to <code>ac_runtime::Error</code>.</li><li><code>HttpServerModule</code> — exposes <code>http_server.*</code> functions.</li><li><code>StubHttpServer</code> — in-memory fake for tests.</li></ul><p><code>HttpServer</code> v1 surface:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>route(method, path, handler)</code></td><td>Register a handler for a method/path pattern.</td></tr><tr><td><code>serve_static(path, dir)</code></td><td>Register a directory of static files.</td></tr><tr><td><code>start(addr)</code></td><td>Start accepting connections on <code>addr</code>. Returns immediately; server runs on its own threads.</td></tr><tr><td><code>stop()</code></td><td>Signal graceful shutdown.</td></tr><tr><td><code>join()</code></td><td>Block until the server has shut down.</td></tr><tr><td><code>is_running()</code></td><td>Whether the server is currently listening.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><code>HttpServerModule</code> v1 function surface (all sync <code>Function</code>s; the server trait hides its internal async I/O):</p><ul><li><code>http_server.new()</code> — create a server value.</li><li><code>http_server.route(server, method, path, handler)</code> — register an handl <code>FunctionValue</code> as the route handler.</li><li><code>http_server.serve_static(server, path, dir)</code> — serve static files from <code>dir</code> under <code>path</code>.</li><li><code>http_server.start(server, addr)</code> — start the server.</li><li><code>http_server.stop(server)</code> — request shutdown.</li><li><code>http_server.join(server)</code> — block until shutdown.</li></ul><h3 id="_4-introduce-handl-lib-http-server-std-concrete-server" tabindex="-1">4. Introduce <code>handl-lib-http-server-std</code> (concrete server) <a class="header-anchor" href="#_4-introduce-handl-lib-http-server-std-concrete-server" aria-label="Permalink to “4. Introduce handl-lib-http-server-std (concrete server)”">​</a></h3><p><code>StdHttpServer</code> is a high-performance, production-baseline implementation:</p><ul><li>Built on <code>tokio</code> + <code>hyper</code> 1.x.</li><li>HTTP/1.1 and HTTP/2 keep-alive.</li><li>Multi-threaded Tokio runtime.</li><li>Trie-based routing with <code>matchit</code> (static and named parameter segments).</li><li>Graceful shutdown with <code>tokio::sync::watch</code> or <code>oneshot</code>.</li><li>Per-request body size limit and timeout.</li><li>Static file serving with path-sanitization and MIME guessing.</li><li>Handler dispatch to handl <code>FunctionValue</code>s via the VM (<code>Context::eval_expr</code> / <code>Context::eval_expr_async</code>) using a per-request fresh <code>Context</code> and the server-owned <code>VirtualMachine</code>.</li></ul><p>Proposed dependencies (stable, well-established versions):</p><ul><li><code>tokio = { version = &quot;1&quot;, features = [&quot;rt-multi-thread&quot;, &quot;macros&quot;, &quot;net&quot;, &quot;time&quot;] }</code></li><li><code>hyper = { version = &quot;1&quot;, features = [&quot;server&quot;, &quot;http1&quot;, &quot;http2&quot;] }</code></li><li><code>hyper-util = { version = &quot;0.1&quot;, features = [&quot;tokio&quot;] }</code></li><li><code>http-body-util = &quot;0.1&quot;</code></li><li><code>matchit = &quot;0.8&quot;</code></li><li><code>mime_guess = &quot;2&quot;</code></li></ul><h3 id="_5-update-the-workspace-cargo-toml" tabindex="-1">5. Update the workspace <code>Cargo.toml</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#_5-update-the-workspace-cargo-toml" aria-label="Permalink to “5. Update the workspace Cargo.toml”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Replace <code>crates/lib-http</code> and <code>crates/lib-http-std</code> with the four new members.</li><li>Add <code>handl-lib-http-client</code> and <code>handl-lib-http-client-std</code> workspace dependency entries.</li><li>Add <code>handl-lib-http-server</code> and <code>handl-lib-http-server-std</code> workspace dependency entries.</li><li>Rename <code>lib-http</code> and <code>lib-http-std</code> feature flags to <code>lib-http-client</code> and <code>lib-http-client-std</code>, and add <code>lib-http-server</code> and <code>lib-http-server-std</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="feature-list-v1" tabindex="-1">Feature List (v1) <a class="header-anchor" href="#feature-list-v1" aria-label="Permalink to “Feature List (v1)”">​</a></h2><h3 id="client-preserved" tabindex="-1">Client (preserved) <a class="header-anchor" href="#client-preserved" aria-label="Permalink to “Client (preserved)”">​</a></h3><ul><li>All existing <code>HttpClient</code> trait methods and <code>HttpClientModule</code> functions.</li><li><code>ureq</code> implementation in <code>lib-http-client-std</code>.</li><li>Stub client for tests.</li></ul><h3 id="server-core" tabindex="-1">Server core <a class="header-anchor" href="#server-core" aria-label="Permalink to “Server core”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Abstract <code>HttpServer</code> trait with lifecycle and routing.</li><li>Request/response value types.</li><li><code>HttpServerError</code> with VM error conversion.</li><li><code>HttpServerModule</code> exposing <code>http_server.*</code> functions to handl.</li><li><code>StubHttpServer</code> for unit tests.</li></ul><h3 id="server-standard-implementation" tabindex="-1">Server standard implementation <a class="header-anchor" href="#server-standard-implementation" aria-label="Permalink to “Server standard implementation”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Tokio/Hyper HTTP/1.1 + HTTP/2 server.</li><li>Graceful start, stop, and join.</li><li>Route matching with <code>{name}</code> path parameters and query strings.</li><li>Middleware/interceptor hook (request/response transform) on the <code>HttpServer</code> trait.</li><li>Static file serving with directory traversal protection.</li><li>Body size and idle timeout limits.</li><li>handl handler dispatch: an handl <code>FunctionValue</code> receives <code>request</code> and returns a response object.</li></ul><h3 id="out-of-scope-for-v1" tabindex="-1">Out of scope for v1 <a class="header-anchor" href="#out-of-scope-for-v1" aria-label="Permalink to “Out of scope for v1”">​</a></h3><ul><li>HTTPS/TLS termination (can be added behind a reverse proxy or in v2).</li><li>WebSockets.</li><li>Request/response streaming bodies (bodies are buffered to strings for v1).</li><li>Compression (<code>gzip</code>, <code>brotli</code>).</li><li>Built-in CORS/rate-limit middleware (pluggable via the middleware hook).</li></ul><h2 id="requirements" tabindex="-1">Requirements <a class="header-anchor" href="#requirements" aria-label="Permalink to “Requirements”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>No breaking changes</strong> to existing handl programs that use <code>http.get</code>, <code>http.post</code>, etc. after the rename.</li><li><strong>No <code>throw</code> in library code</strong> — all errors are returned as <code>Result</code> and converted to <code>ac_runtime::Error</code> at the module boundary.</li><li><strong>Async capability</strong> — the server I/O is async, but the module functions remain sync so they work with the current <code>Function</code> trait. The implementation runs the server on a background Tokio runtime and communicates via channels.</li><li><strong>Thread safety</strong> — <code>HttpServer</code> and <code>HttpServerModule</code> must be <code>Send + Sync</code>.</li><li><strong>Testability</strong> — every public function has a unit test; <code>StdHttpServer</code> has an integration test that starts a server and makes real HTTP requests.</li><li><strong>Documentation</strong> — each crate has an updated top-level module doc and <code>README.md</code>.</li></ol><h2 id="test-plan" tabindex="-1">Test Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#test-plan" aria-label="Permalink to “Test Plan”">​</a></h2><h3 id="crates-lib-http-client" tabindex="-1"><code>crates/lib-http-client</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#crates-lib-http-client" aria-label="Permalink to “crates/lib-http-client”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Keep/rewrite existing <code>http_client_tests.rs</code> and <code>error_tests.rs</code> under the new path.</li><li>Add a rename regression test that imports <code>handl_lib_http_client</code> and calls <code>HttpClientModule::new(StubHttpClient)</code>.</li></ul><h3 id="crates-lib-http-client-std" tabindex="-1"><code>crates/lib-http-client-std</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#crates-lib-http-client-std" aria-label="Permalink to “crates/lib-http-client-std”">​</a></h3><ul><li>Keep/rewrite existing <code>ureq</code> implementation tests.</li><li>Optionally add a tiny real network smoke test behind a feature flag (<code>network_tests</code>).</li></ul><h3 id="crates-lib-http-server" tabindex="-1"><code>crates/lib-http-server</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#crates-lib-http-server" aria-label="Permalink to “crates/lib-http-server”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>src/http_server/http_server_stub.rs</code> — stub implementation returning canned responses.</li><li><code>src/http_server/http_server_tests.rs</code> — module tests for <code>http_server.new</code>, <code>route</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>join</code> with the stub.</li><li><code>src/route/route_tests.rs</code> — route matching (static, parameters, 404, method mismatch).</li><li><code>src/request/request_tests.rs</code> — query parsing, header extraction.</li><li><code>src/error/error_tests.rs</code> — <code>HttpServerError</code> display and VM conversion.</li></ul><h3 id="crates-lib-http-server-std" tabindex="-1"><code>crates/lib-http-server-std</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#crates-lib-http-server-std" aria-label="Permalink to “crates/lib-http-server-std”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>src/http_server/std_tests.rs</code> — unit tests for <code>StdHttpServer</code> using the stub.</li><li><code>tests/integration_tests.rs</code> — start <code>StdHttpServer</code> on <code>127.0.0.1:0</code>, make a request with a small test client, assert status/body/headers, then <code>stop</code> and <code>join</code>.</li></ul><h3 id="crates-runtime-core" tabindex="-1"><code>crates/runtime-core</code> <a class="header-anchor" href="#crates-runtime-core" aria-label="Permalink to “crates/runtime-core”">​</a></h3><ul><li><code>src/module/module_tests.rs</code> — add tests that an <code>AsyncFunction</code> and an <code>Operation</code> registered through a <code>Module</code> are dispatched by <code>ModuleHost</code>.</li></ul><h2 id="implementation-phases" tabindex="-1">Implementation Phases <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation-phases" aria-label="Permalink to “Implementation Phases”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>P0: Module async/operation dispatch</strong> — unblock server module from exposing async functions and operations.</li><li><strong>P1: Rename client crates</strong> — <code>lib-http</code> → <code>lib-http-client</code>, <code>lib-http-std</code> → <code>lib-http-client-std</code>; update workspace and feature flags; run <code>cargo check</code> and tests.</li><li><strong>P2: Abstract server crate</strong> — create <code>lib-http-server</code> with trait, types, error, module adapter, stub, and tests.</li><li><strong>P3: Standard server crate</strong> — create <code>lib-http-server-std</code> with <code>StdHttpServer</code> (tokio/hyper), routing, static files, handl handler dispatch, and integration tests.</li><li><strong>P4: Workspace integration</strong> — add server feature flags to the root <code>handl</code> crate, update <code>README.md</code>, and run <code>cargo test -p handl-lib-http-client -p handl-lib-http-client-std -p handl-lib-http-server -p handl-lib-http-server-std</code>.</li></ol><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li>The HTTP surface is split into client and server, making the capability names honest and future-proof.</li><li>handl programs can author HTTP servers by registering routes and handlers, then calling <code>http_server.start</code>.</li><li>New runtime dependencies (<code>tokio</code>, <code>hyper</code>, <code>matchit</code>, <code>mime_guess</code>) are isolated in <code>lib-http-server-std</code>.</li><li>The <code>Module</code>/<code>ModuleHost</code> changes benefit all future async modules (<code>fs</code>, <code>kv</code>, etc.).</li><li>handl server performance is bounded by the synchronous, per-request VM evaluation; v1 is production-capable for I/O, and handler throughput can be optimized later with VM caching or pre-compiled continuations.</li></ul><h2 id="v1-completion-notes" tabindex="-1">v1 Completion Notes <a class="header-anchor" href="#v1-completion-notes" aria-label="Permalink to “v1 Completion Notes”">​</a></h2><p>The HTTP client/server split and production-baseline server are implemented and tested.</p><ul><li>P0: <code>Module</code> and <code>ModuleHost</code> now dispatch <code>AsyncFunction</code> and <code>Operation</code>; tests added.</li><li>P1: Renamed <code>lib-http</code> → <code>lib-http-client</code> and <code>lib-http-std</code> → <code>lib-http-client-std</code>; updated workspace members, dependencies, and feature flags.</li><li>P2: Created <code>handl-lib-http-server</code> with the <code>HttpServer</code> trait, <code>HttpServerModule</code>, <code>HttpServerRequest</code>/<code>HttpServerResponse</code>, <code>HttpServerError</code>, and <code>StubHttpServer</code> tests.</li><li>P3: Created <code>handl-lib-http-server-std</code> with <code>StdHttpServer</code> (tokio + hyper HTTP/1.1), <code>ServerConfig</code> (body limit, idle timeout, keep-alive), request body size enforcement, idle timeout, <code>JoinSet</code>-based graceful shutdown, <code>mime_guess</code> for static files, and default <code>Content-Type</code> for handler responses.</li><li><code>cargo test</code> passes for <code>handl-lib-http-client</code>, <code>handl-lib-http-client-std</code>, <code>handl-lib-http-server</code>, <code>handl-lib-http-server-std</code>, and <code>handl-runtime-modules</code>.</li></ul>`,55)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};